# Cursor Rules for thiru.site

## Design Principles

### 1. Minimal Design
- Prefer simple, clean layouts over complex visual elements
- Avoid excessive spacing and visual clutter
- Focus on content readability and accessibility

### 2. Content-First Approach
- Prioritize content over decorative elements
- Use the `prose` class for all content pages
- Ensure content is easily scannable and readable

### 3. No Redundant Navigation
- Don't include page headings (h1) when navbar already provides navigation context
- The navbar should be the primary navigation indicator
- Avoid duplicate navigation information

### 4. Consistent Styling
- Use the `prose` class for all content pages
- Use `simple-list` class for clean list presentations
- Maintain consistent typography and spacing across pages

### 5. Compact Layouts
- Prefer compact, efficient layouts over spacious designs
- Use minimal spacing between elements
- Avoid unnecessary visual separation

## Development Guidelines

### 6. No Content Duplication
- Avoid duplicate content across pages
- Merge similar pages when appropriate (e.g., About + Experience)
- Keep content focused and purposeful

### 7. Simple Component Structure
- Prefer simple HTML structure over complex layouts
- Use semantic HTML elements appropriately
- Avoid unnecessary wrapper divs and containers

### 8. Performance Considerations
- Remove unused components and complexity
- Prefer simple CSS over complex animations
- Optimize for fast loading and rendering

### 9. Mobile-First Design
- Ensure all layouts work well on mobile devices
- Use responsive design principles
- Test layouts on different screen sizes

### 10. Accessibility
- Use proper alt text for images
- Ensure proper heading hierarchy
- Maintain good color contrast
- Use semantic HTML elements

## Code Style

### 11. React/Next.js Best Practices
- Use Client Components only when necessary (for interactivity)
- Prefer Server Components for static content
- Use proper TypeScript types
- Follow Next.js 13+ App Router conventions

### 12. CSS Guidelines
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Prefer simple CSS over complex custom styles
- Use CSS custom properties for theming
- Maintain consistent spacing and sizing

### 13. File Organization
- Keep components simple and focused
- Use descriptive file and component names
- Organize code logically and consistently

## Content Guidelines

### 14. Writing Style
- Keep content concise and focused
- Use clear, professional language
- Avoid unnecessary jargon
- Write for the target audience

### 15. Information Architecture
- Organize content logically
- Use clear navigation structure
- Ensure content is easy to find and access
- Maintain consistent content patterns

## Quality Assurance

### 16. Testing
- Ensure all links work correctly
- Test responsive design on multiple devices
- Verify accessibility compliance
- Check for broken images or resources

### 17. Performance
- Optimize images and assets
- Minimize bundle size
- Use efficient loading strategies
- Monitor Core Web Vitals

### 18. Maintenance
- Keep dependencies updated
- Remove unused code and files
- Document important decisions
- Maintain clean git history 